darwin stall: No audio from the player for 10 s. If macOS asks to let Spytify record system audio, allow it; it is in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Screen & System Audio Recording.
darwin call: The player's output device runs at 16 kHz mono, not fit for recording: tracks will sound like a phone call. A Bluetooth headset switches to call mode when an app opens its microphone. In System Settings > Sound > Input, choose another microphone, such as the built-in one, or play to another output.
darwin 8 kHz: The player's output device runs at 8 kHz, not fit for recording: tracks will sound like a phone call. A Bluetooth headset switches to call mode when an app opens its microphone. In System Settings > Sound > Input, choose another microphone, such as the built-in one, or play to another output.
windows stall: No audio from the player for 10 s. Check that the Windows Audio service runs and that the player plays on an output device.
windows call: The player's output device runs at 16 kHz mono, not fit for recording: tracks will sound like a phone call. A Bluetooth headset does this while an app uses its microphone. Choose another output in Settings > System > Sound, or end what uses the headset's microphone.
windows 8 kHz: The player's output device runs at 8 kHz, not fit for recording: tracks will sound like a phone call. A Bluetooth headset does this while an app uses its microphone. Choose another output in Settings > System > Sound, or end what uses the headset's microphone.
linux stall: No audio from the player for 10 s. Check that PipeWire runs: systemctl --user restart pipewire.
linux call: The player's output device runs at 16 kHz mono, not fit for recording: tracks will sound like a phone call. A Bluetooth headset does this while an app uses its microphone. Choose another output device, or end what uses the headset's microphone.
linux 8 kHz: The player's output device runs at 8 kHz, not fit for recording: tracks will sound like a phone call. A Bluetooth headset does this while an app uses its microphone. Choose another output device, or end what uses the headset's microphone.
